# Playwright Conventions

Full standard for Didaxis Playwright tests. Auto-attaches on `tests/**`.

## 1. Locators

User-facing locators only, in priority order: `getByRole` → `getByLabel` / `getByPlaceholder` → `getByText` → `getByTestId` (escape hatch + why). Never CSS, XPath, or brittle text. Ambiguous matches use `.filter({ hasText })`, not `.first()`.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — from pages/ProgramsPage.ts
this.newProgramButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: '+ New Program' });
return this.page.getByRole('row').filter({
  has: this.page.getByRole('cell').getByText(programName, { exact: true }),
});
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
page.locator('.btn-primary');
page.locator('//button[1]');
programs.programRow(name).first();
```

**Why:** CSS/XPath and `.first()` break when the DOM or row order shifts — the leading cause of selector flake.

> **Advise:** If you must use `getByTestId`, comment why role/label/placeholder/text failed (no example in-repo yet).

## 2. Waiting

Never `waitForTimeout`. Use web-first expects that retry: `toBeVisible()` / `toBeEnabled()` / `toHaveText()`. Never `expect(await locator.isVisible()).toBe(true)`.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — from tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts
await expect(programs.programRow(programName)).toBeVisible();
await expect(modal.createButton).toBeDisabled();
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad — waitForTimeout still appears in tests/ds4-create-program.spec.ts
await page.waitForTimeout(500);
await expect(await modal.dialog.isVisible()).toBe(true);
```

**Why:** Fixed sleeps race the UI; snapshot booleans do not auto-retry — both cause intermittent timeouts.

## 3. Page Objects

All UI goes through POMs in `pages/`. One class per page/component; locators are `readonly` in the constructor; methods act, never assert. Specs describe intent and hold no inline locators.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — from tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts + pages/ProgramsPage.ts
const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
await programs.goto();
await programs.openNewProgramForm();
await expect(programs.newProgramModal.heading).toBeVisible();
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
await page.getByRole('button', { name: '+ New Program' }).click();
// inside ProgramsPage:
async openNewProgramForm() {
  await this.newProgramButton.click();
  await expect(this.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeVisible(); // assertion in POM
}
```

**Why:** Inline locators and POM asserts duplicate logic and hide intent — failures become hard to triage and fix once.

## 4. Auth

Default: stored session from setup (`auth.setup.ts` → `playwright/.auth/user.json`). Login-page tests only: empty `storageState` + UI login. API login for bulk setup / stale state.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — chromium project in playwright.config.ts (storageState + setup dependency)
{
  name: 'chromium',
  use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'], storageState: 'playwright/.auth/user.json' },
  dependencies: ['setup'],
}
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad — UI login in every feature test
test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.getByLabel('Email').fill(email);
  await page.getByLabel('Password').fill(password);
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign In' }).click();
});
```

**Why:** Per-test UI login adds minutes of flake surface (redirects, cookies, race on Sign In) that storageState removes.

> **Advise:** For a dedicated login-page spec, use `test.use({ storageState: { cookies: [], origins: [] } })` then exercise UI login (pattern in `auth-strategy.md`; no dedicated login-page a11y/login spec wired that way yet).

## 5. Test data

Unique names via `uniqueName()` / `Date.now()`. Import `test` from `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts`. Call `trackProgram(uuid)` as soon as a program exists. Fixture deletes via API — no manual `afterAll` / UI teardown. Never hardcode tokens; never delete data you did not create.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — from tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from '../fixtures/cleanup.fixture';
const programName = uniqueName('Web Development 2026');
trackProgram(await createProgramReturningId(page, programName, description));
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
const programName = 'Web Development 2026'; // collides across workers
test.afterAll(async ({ page }) => { await page.getByRole('button', { name: /Delete/ }).click(); });
```

**Why:** Shared names and leftover programs collide under `fullyParallel` and poison later runs.

## 6. API testing

Prefer Playwright `request` for setup/teardown and contract checks. Capture create UUIDs from POST responses. Never mock the endpoint under test when verifying the real API.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — pattern from cleanup fixture + helpers (wait for real POST, track id)
trackProgram(await createProgramReturningId(page, programName, description));
// DELETE /api/programs/<uuid> runs in the fixture teardown
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
await page.route('**/api/programs**', (route) =>
  route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ id: 'fake' }) }),
); // while asserting "program was saved to the API"
```

**Why:** Mocking the endpoint under test turns a contract check into a tautology — real regressions pass green.

> **Advise:** For pure API-only checks, use `request.post/get/delete` against `/api/programs` with env auth (no in-repo example that drives the full flow via `request` alone yet).

## 7. Network mocking

Use `page.route` for deterministic UI reactions: (a) POST 503 → error UI; (b) GET 200 `[]` → empty-state; (c) 200 malformed → no crash; plus 401/403/404/500/501/502/300/timeout. Observe real copy first — never invent strings. POMs only; one tag per test.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — from tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts (POST failure; assert UI still open / row absent)
await page.route('**/api/programs**', async (route) => {
  if (route.request().method() === 'POST') {
    await route.fulfill({
      status: 500,
      contentType: 'application/json',
      body: JSON.stringify({ error: 'Internal Server Error' }),
    });
    return;
  }
  await route.continue();
});
await programs.openNewProgramForm();
// … assert observed error / modal state — copy from live UI
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
await expect(page.getByText('Something went wrong, please retry later')).toBeVisible();
// invented string; never observed on the real app
```

**Why:** Live API errors are non-deterministic; invented copy fails when the product wording differs.

## 8. Accessibility

Axe with `.withTags(['wcag2a','wcag2aa'])` then `expect(results.violations).toEqual([])`. `.include()` / `.exclude()` only for noisy third-party widgets (comment why). Keyboard: tab → `toBeFocused()` → Enter → dialog opens via POMs. One tag per test. Real violations → report and stop; never `.disableRules()` to go green.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — advise aligning tests/programs.a11y.spec.ts to this shape
const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page })
  .withTags(['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa'])
  .analyze();
await expect(results.violations).toEqual([]);
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad — current tests/programs.a11y.spec.ts still does this on the modal scan
const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page })
  .include(await programs.newProgramModal.axeIncludeSelector())
  .disableRules(['button-name']) // silences a real naming violation
  .analyze();
```

**Why:** `.disableRules()` to go green hides WCAG defects users hit; untagged scans miss A/AA rules this project requires.

> **Advise:** Add a keyboard test (no in-repo example yet): tab to `programs.newProgramButton` → `toBeFocused()` → Enter → `expect(programs.newProgramModal.dialog).toBeVisible()`.

## 9. Assertions

Web-first expects in the spec only. Use `expect.soft` for independent multi-checks. `toHaveScreenshot` only when visual regression is intentional. Relative timestamps: `page.clock.install` before navigate.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — web-first (from specs); soft + clock advised
await expect(programs.programRow(programName)).toBeVisible();
await expect.soft(programs.programDescription(programName, description)).toBeVisible();
await expect.soft(programs.editButton(programName)).toBeVisible();
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
expect(await programs.programRow(programName).count()).toBe(1); // no auto-retry
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot(); // without an intentional visual contract
```

**Why:** Non-retrying asserts flake on slow paint; accidental screenshots fail on font/OS drift.

> **Advise:** No `expect.soft` or `page.clock.install` usage in-repo yet — when asserting “5 minutes ago”, freeze time first:
> `await page.clock.install({ time: new Date('2026-03-15T15:00:00.000Z') });`

## 10. Anti-flake

Config: `fullyParallel: true`; `retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0`; `baseURL` from env; `trace: 'on-first-retry'`; pinned `locale` / `timezoneId` once set. Never raise retries above 2; never set `workers: 1`. Prefer better locators/waits/clock/mocks over more retries.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — playwright.config.ts
fullyParallel: true,
retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,
use: { baseURL: process.env.DIDAXIS_URL, trace: 'on-first-retry' },
```

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
retries: process.env.CI ? 5 : 2,
workers: 1,
await page.waitForTimeout(3000); // "stabilize" instead of fixing the wait
```

**Why:** High retries and serial workers hide flake and slow the suite; sleeps paper over races instead of fixing them.

---

## Do / Don't

| Do | Don't |
|---|---|
| `getByRole` → label/placeholder → text → `getByTestId`+why | CSS, XPath, brittle text, `.first()` |
| `expect(locator).toBeVisible()` | `waitForTimeout`, `expect(await isVisible()).toBe(true)` |
| Drive UI via `pages/` POMs | Inline locators or `expect` inside POMs |
| storageState / setup for feature tests | UI login in every `beforeEach` |
| `uniqueName` + `trackProgram` via cleanup fixture | Shared names, UI/`afterAll` teardown |
| Real API for contracts; `request` for setup | Mock the endpoint under test |
| `page.route` after observing real UI copy | Invented error/empty strings |
| Axe `wcag2a`/`wcag2aa` + keyboard path | `.disableRules()` to go green |
| Web-first / `expect.soft` / `page.clock` | Snapshot booleans, wall-clock relative time |
| CI retries ≤ 2, keep parallelism | `retries > 2` or `workers: 1` |

## Refusals (hard stops)

The agent must **refuse** these requests — stop, do not apply the change, and
raise the conflict to the user:

- **Weaken or delete an assertion to make a test pass** — refuse; fix the
  locator, wait, mock, or file an app bug instead.
- **Heal a failure triage classified as a real app bug** — refuse; route to
  bug-reporter. Self-heal is for drift only.
- **Replace a role-based locator with CSS or XPath** — refuse; re-discover via
  `getByRole` → label/placeholder → text → `getByTestId`.
- **Use `waitForTimeout`** — refuse; use web-first `expect(locator)` retries.
- **Hardcode a credential** (password, token, API key) — refuse; use env vars,
  `storageState`, or fixture setup.
- **Use the `any` type** — refuse; add or infer a proper type.
